.TH ZENITHCTL 1 "October 2026" "Zenith 1.2.0" "User Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
zenithctl \- CLI and interactive TUI control utility for Zenith Gaming Daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zenithctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zenithctl
is the primary user-facing interface for controlling, inspecting, diagnosing, and monitoring the
.B zenith
gaming optimization daemon via its local UNIX domain socket (\fI/run/zenith/zenith.sock\fR).
.PP
It allows non-root users (belonging to group \fBzenith\fR or \fBwheel\fR) to switch profiles, inspect real-time topology, diagnose system health, generate anonymized support reports, and monitor active gaming sessions in a live Terminal User Interface (TUI).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [\-\-watch]
Display current daemon status, detected games, active profile, and applied tweaks.
If \fB\-\-watch\fR is passed, launches an interactive live TUI dashboard displaying CPU topology (CCD/P/E cores), PSI memory/CPU pressure, GPU temperatures, and recent events.
.TP
.B enable
Enable dynamic game optimizations in the running daemon.
.TP
.B disable
Disable game optimizations and restore all system parameters to their original baseline.
.TP
.B profile list
List all available optimization profiles (\fBsafe\fR, \fBbalanced\fR, \fBaggressive\fR) and show which is currently active.
.TP
.B profile set \fINAME\fR
Switch the active profile to \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B game list
List all currently running detected gaming processes and their associated PIDs and CCD pinnings.
.TP
.B game add \fIPID\fR [\-\-profile \fIPROF\fR]
Manually register process \fIPID\fR as an active game session.
.TP
.B doctor
Run comprehensive environment diagnostic check (cgroups v2, kernel version, drivers, conflicting services like GameMode/tuned/auto-cpufreq, AMD 3D V-Cache driver, NVML, PSI). Outputs pass/warn/fail status with actionable remediation commands.
.TP
.B explain [\fITWEAK_NAME\fR]
Explain the scientific rationale, kernel paths, risks, and benefits of one or all tweaks.
.TP
.B rollback
Force an immediate emergency rollback of all recorded mutations via the daemon socket.
.TP
.B report [\-\-redact]
Generate a standardized diagnostic support bundle for bug reporting. If \fB\-\-redact\fR is provided, sanitizes usernames, hostnames, and IP addresses.
.TP
.B logs [\-n \fICOUNT\fR] [\-\-json]
Display recent structured log entries recorded by the daemon.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell autocompletion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, or \fBfish\fR.
.TP
.B version
Print daemon and client version information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Override default UNIX domain socket path (\fI/run/zenith/zenith.sock\fR).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Format output as machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage instructions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Launch interactive real-time TUI dashboard:
.RS
.B zenithctl status \-\-watch
.RE
.PP
Run diagnostic self-check and identify conflicting services:
.RS
.B zenithctl doctor
.RE
.PP
Switch active profile to aggressive:
.RS
.B zenithctl profile set aggressive
.RE
.PP
Generate shell completions for zsh:
.RS
.B zenithctl completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_zenithctl
.RE
